{%- assign scheme = site.data.colorscheme[site.default_scheme] -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Firefox and chromium have two different quirks regarding dynamic favicons.

  Firefox does not support media queries in <link>, so we need to use @media inside style inside the svg instead.
  Chromium supports both query locations, but it rasterizes the svg upon loading it, so it doesn't switch modes without a reload.

  To satisfy both: we make a svg with @media query inside, and put that same SVG in two different <link> with dark/light media queries.
  Chromium caches by URI, so we put a space right before one of the SVGs to cache bust
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- capture svg_raw -%}
<svg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' viewBox='0 0 32 32'>
  <style>
    path { fill: {{ scheme.colors.light.primary }}; }
    @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
      path { fill: {{ scheme.colors.dark.primary }}; }
    }
  </style>
  <path d='M16,1L21,11L31,16L21,21L16,31L11,21L1,16L11,11Z'/>
</svg>
{%- endcapture -%}
{% assign svg = svg_raw | url_encode | replace: '+', '%20' %}

<link rel="icon" media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)" href="data:image/svg+xml, {{ svg }}">
<link rel="icon" media="(prefers-color-scheme: light)" href="data:image/svg+xml,{{ svg }}">
